        {
          "id": 1061282551,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Sure. I added one (tcp-exp-option-tarr.pcap.gz). Please note that this does not provide a valid packet exchange: It is generated using packetdrill and one side does not announce support for it, but the other side sends the option anyway. However, for testing the support of the option in wireshark, this trace is perfectly fine.\nPlease note that I'll add support for the TARR option soon in a separate commit. I can also update tcp-exp-option-tarr.pcap.gz to a valid packet exchange, once I have a working implementation in FreeBSD.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6767546,
            "username": "tuexen",
